<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">S1. Compliance Model Specification</h3>

<div id="A1.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Compliance with the forced-choice response format was modeled using hierarchical Bayesian logistic regression. The binary outcome variable indicated whether a model produced a valid structured response (“A” or “B”).</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SSx1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SSx1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{ijkl}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{ijkl}</annotation></semantics></math> denote compliance for trial <math id="A1.SSx1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> from model <math id="A1.SSx1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, IAT domain <math id="A1.SSx1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, block <math id="A1.SSx1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>, and item <math id="A1.SSx1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>. The model was specified as:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{ijkl}\sim\text{Bernoulli}(p_{ijkl})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Bernoulli</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{ijkl}\sim\text{Bernoulli}(p_{ijkl})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{logit}(p_{ijkl})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>logit</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{logit}(p_{ijkl})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta_{0}+\beta_{1}\text{Block}_{l}+\beta_{2}\text{Model}_{j}+\beta_{3}\text{Domain}_{k}+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>Block</mtext><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>Model</mtext><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>Domain</mtext><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta_{0}+\beta_{1}\text{Block}_{l}+\beta_{2}\text{Model}_{j}+\beta_{3}\text{Domain}_{k}+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta_{4}(\text{Block}\times\text{Model})+\beta_{5}(\text{Block}\times\text{Domain})+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Block</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext>Model</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Block</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext>Domain</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta_{4}(\text{Block}\times\text{Model})+\beta_{5}(\text{Block}\times\text{Domain})+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta_{6}(\text{Model}\times\text{Domain})+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Model</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext>Domain</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta_{6}(\text{Model}\times\text{Domain})+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta_{7}(\text{Block}\times\text{Model}\times\text{Domain})+u_{m}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Block</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext>Model</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext>Domain</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta_{7}(\text{Block}\times\text{Model}\times\text{Domain})+u_{m},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SSx1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SSx1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{m}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma_{\text{item}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>item</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{m}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma_{\text{item}})</annotation></semantics></math> represents item-level random intercepts capturing stimulus-specific compliance heterogeneity.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SSx2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">S2. Prior Specification</h3>

<div id="A1.SSx2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Weakly regularizing priors were used to stabilize estimation while allowing the data to dominate inference.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SSx2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Fixed effects were assigned:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{r}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{r}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SSx2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">reflecting the expectation that large log-odds effects are unlikely but not impossible.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SSx2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The intercept was assigned:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{0}\sim\mathcal{N}(3,1.5)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{0}\sim\mathcal{N}(3,1.5)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SSx2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">corresponding to a broad prior expectation of high compliance (centered near 95% probability) without enforcing near-deterministic behavior.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SSx2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">The item-level standard deviation was assigned:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx2.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\text{item}}\sim\text{Exponential}(1)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>item</mtext></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Exponential</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\text{item}}\sim\text{Exponential}(1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx2.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SSx2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">a weakly informative prior favoring moderate variability while permitting larger dispersion if supported by the data.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SSx3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">S3. Posterior Estimation</h3>

<div id="A1.SSx3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SSx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Models were fit using Hamiltonian Monte Carlo (No-U-Turn Sampler) as implemented in <span id="A1.SSx3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">brms</span> and Stan. Four chains were run for 4,000 iterations each, with 1,500 warm-up iterations per chain, yielding 10,000 post-warmup draws.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SSx3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Posterior summaries are reported as means with 95% credible intervals, in Table <a href="#A1.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ S3. Posterior Estimation ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ A Two-Stage Statistical Framework for Evaluating Associative Interference in Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. Raw observed rates are provided in Table <a href="#A1.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ S4. Convergence Diagnostics ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ A Two-Stage Statistical Framework for Evaluating Associative Interference in Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T2" class="ltx_table">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Posterior predicted compliance probability (%) by model and IAT domain. Values are means with 95% credible intervals.</figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
